              <p>Hello fellow hams,</p>

              <p>
                The July fox hunt is tomorrow! Here are the final
                details for the <strong>July Practice Hunt</strong>
                at <strong>Flaming Geyser State Park</strong>.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:20px 0 8px;">
                Logistics
              </h3>
              <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
                     border="0"
                     style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;">
                <tr>
                  <td width="140"
                      style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Meet time:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Noon</strong> at the main picnic
                    area near the park entrance
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Address:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    23700 SE Flaming Geyser Rd,
                    Auburn, WA&nbsp;98092
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Parking:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Discover Pass required.</strong>
                    Day-use fee is $10 at the kiosk if you
                    do not have an annual pass.
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Frequency:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex</strong>
                    (callsign K7LED)
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Wrap-up:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    2:00&nbsp;PM &mdash; post-hunt debrief at
                    the picnic area
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:20px 0 8px;">
                Last-Minute Reminders
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Program your HT to
                  <strong>147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex</strong>
                  tonight
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Bring your <strong>Discover Pass</strong>
                  or $10 cash for day-use parking
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Check the weather; dress in layers and bring
                  rain gear if there is a chance of showers
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Bring water and a snack; trail shoes
                  recommended
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                No experience needed &mdash; just show up at
                noon and we will get you started. Loaner radios
                and Yagi antennas are available.
              </p>

              <p>
                Questions tonight? Contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                [TOM-EMAIL].
              </p>

              <p>
                See you on the hunt! 73 de KE4HET
              </p>

